From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: KmsModeSet <kmsmodeset@local>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 19:00:00 
Subject: [PATCH 0109] gpu31-kms: give the DSI encoder a mode_set hook (int67, module-only)

int66 reaches the first modeset and then jumps to NULL:

    PC is at 0x0
    LR is at crtc_set_mode.isra.0+0x144 [drm_kms_helper]

drm_atomic_helper's crtc_set_mode() in this tree calls
`encoder->funcs->mode_set(encoder, mode, adjusted_mode)` unconditionally
(drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_helper.c:753); this encoder only had .disable and
.mode_fixup.  The DSI link and DECON programming live in the CRTC
(enable_link()), so the encoder hook is a logging no-op.

Audit of the other hooks the helper calls around a modeset (same file), so the
next one is not hit blind:

  - encoder .prepare/.disable/.dpms: guarded, and .disable exists here, so the
    else-chain never reaches .dpms;
  - encoder .enable/.commit: `if (funcs->enable) ... else if (funcs->commit)`,
    both optional (neither is set);
  - encoder .mode_fixup: called when .atomic_check is absent (it is), and it
    exists;
  - CRTC .mode_set/.mode_fixup/.disable/.enable: guarded / implemented;
  - only the encoder .mode_set call is unguarded.

Module-only change: only drivers/gpu/drm/exynos7580/exynos_drm7580_dsi.c is
touched, which is not part of the built-in image.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos7580/exynos_drm7580_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/exynos7580/exynos_drm7580_dsi.c
@@ -161,6 +161,23 @@
 }
 
 /*
+ * int67: drm_atomic_helper's crtc_set_mode() calls encoder->funcs->mode_set()
+ * unconditionally (drivers/gpu/drm/drm_atomic_helper.c:753 in this tree), and
+ * this encoder had no such callback, so the first modeset jumped to NULL.
+ * The DSI link and DECON programming live in the CRTC (enable_link()), so the
+ * encoder hook is a logging no-op, as in the upstream drivers.
+ */
+static void
+exynos7580_dsi_encoder_mode_set(struct drm_encoder *encoder,
+				struct drm_display_mode *mode,
+				struct drm_display_mode *adjusted_mode)
+{
+	DRM_DEBUG_KMS("DSI encoder: mode_set %ux%u@%u (link handled by CRTC)\n",
+		      adjusted_mode->hdisplay, adjusted_mode->vdisplay,
+		      drm_mode_vrefresh(adjusted_mode));
+}
+
+/*
  * The CRTC hands us the requested mode; reject anything but the panel timing
  * and give the CRTC the exact values it must program into DECON and DSIM, so
  * a userspace-supplied variant of the same mode cannot slip through.
@@ -184,6 +201,7 @@
 static const struct drm_encoder_helper_funcs exynos7580_dsi_encoder_helper_funcs = {
 	.disable	= exynos7580_dsi_encoder_disable,
 	.mode_fixup	= exynos7580_dsi_encoder_mode_fixup,
+	.mode_set	= exynos7580_dsi_encoder_mode_set,
 };
 
 static const struct drm_encoder_funcs exynos7580_dsi_encoder_funcs = {
